    "created_at": "2016-02-01T16:46:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-01T16:51:35Z",
    "body": "We have recurring requests / bug reports about imprecise seeking, especially when clients target frame boundaries, and the only real solution is some kind of rational time based seeking.  That's something I've been interested in for a while: https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-whatwg-archive/2012Oct/0013.html\n\nAside from more \"professional\" use cases like \"web based video editors\" and the like, we've recently seen these kinds of bugs crop up, e.g., when people want to synchronize the page's scroll position with a specific frame in a &lt;video&gt; element, and they have trouble seeking to the correct frame.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
