    "created_at": "2016-02-01T17:08:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-01T17:08:06Z",
    "body": "Hmm, what happens if one tries to seek to the middle of a frame instead? I realize that only rational numbers are going to _really_ fix the problem, though.\n\nAbove I just wanted to make sure that a new `seek()` doesn't ruin the possibility of rational-time seeking. If you'd like to work on that, can you create a new issue and summarize what needs to be done? (I'd then redirect the legacy bugs there.) Pull requests welcome too, of course, but feedback from some of Google, Mozilla and Microsoft would be nice first.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
