    "created_at": "2016-02-02T17:11:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-02T17:19:23Z",
    "body": "> Hmm, what happens if one tries to seek to the middle of a frame instead?\n\nYou seek to somewhere near the middle of the frame, but the frame only plays for 1/2 its duration. Authors could also just add a small mantissa value to bias the rounding in the direction they want.  But as you note, the only real way to solve the problem is by supporting rational time values.\n\n> If you'd like to work on that, can you create a new issue and summarize what needs to be done?\n\nI can do that. Building off your `SeekOptions` dictionary, it may be as simple as adding a `timeScale` option: `video.seek(30 * 1001, {mode:\"precise\", timeScale:30000});` to seek to the 30th frame of a 29.97 fps video.  For the initial feature, the time scale for the movie would have to be provided out of band, while we work on some way of exposing the movie's natural time scale to script.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
