    "created_at": "2016-02-03T19:57:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-03T19:57:43Z",
    "body": "Firefox's (precise) seek implementation can seek to individual audio frame boundaries, modulo rounding issues caused by storing the seek target in a double in JS and then converting it to int64_t microseconds, which is generally the time format our media stack uses internally.\n\nWe've had a few bugs filed over the years about seeking to video frames not working thanks to said rounding issues. We've never felt it a huge priority to address that, but I'd be happy to leave scope in the spec to handle that in future.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
